{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/693975-theatre-of-shadows-mush-owod-vampire-focused-mush-seeks-staff-players","id":693975,"title":"Theatre of Shadows MUSH - OWoD Vampire-focused MUSH Seeks Staff/Players","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-08T10:04:56-07:00","id":693975,"title":"Theatre of Shadows MUSH - OWoD Vampire-focused MUSH Seeks Staff/Players","content":"Good evening all. There's a lot of online vampire players here; I figured I would share information about my current project. <hr /><br /> Theatre of Shadows MUSH is an in-development Vampire the Masquerade MUSH (online text-based roleplaying game) set in the modern nights, focusing on the Camarilla, Anarch Movement and Independent/Autarkis Kindred in an original city in Northern California. We are drawing inspiration from a number of sources, primarily the themes and stylings of Vampire the Masquerade, but also such media as The Vampire Chronicles, Dark Shadows, American Gothic, Fringe, Forever Knight, Supernatural, Buffy the Vampire Slayer/Angel and others. We will be endeavoring to create a world that focuses on two primary elements: gothic horror and supernatural intrigue, though these won't be the only stories to be told, not by far.<br /> <br /> The MUSH has been slowly, but steadily approaching the end of the development cycle, and it's the perfect time to get in on the ground floor. We utilize the new Mind's Eye Theatre: Vampire the Masquerade by By Night Studios for our system, easy to use but with a lot of depth, with a series of house rules that fix a small number of oversights or problems that we have found in more than 2 years of live-action, focused play. You can find our current website, an under-construction wiki with current policies and other info at <a href=\"http://www.theatremush.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.theatremush.com/</a><br /> <br /> Our goal with this MUSH is to give a focused, story- and plot-driven experience, with plots that range from local focus in the city, but also have interaction with and effect on the larger World of Darkness. There is also a great deal of long-term consideration for the metaplot of Vampire the Masquerade and how the players might interact with and effect that. The game will take the Vampire the Masquerade world and update it to the modern nights, using elements of Revised, V20 and By Night Studios' default timeline.<br /> <br /> Of particular note:<ul><li>Gehenna has not happened (and likely not started beyond a couple of corner case events)</li> <li>The Assamite Schism happened and the Schismatic Assamites are recognized as a Pillar Clan of the Camarilla, with Tegyrius as their Justicar, having Primogen in most cities.</li> <li>The Gangrel split on leaving, now recognized as a Lesser Clan of the Camarilla (and in some cases, trying to regain their Pillar status), their representation on city courts with Primogen stripped long ago. About a third of the Gangrel stayed with the Camarilla, the rest leaving at Xaviar's behest.</li> <li>The Week of Nightmares has not happened.</li> <li>The Sabbat War has cooled down in many areas, though the most hotly-contested territory still is (NYC, for example).</li> <li>The Giovanni and Followers of Set have the beginnings of a clandestine alliance in the face of an expanded Camarilla, the Loyalist Assamites under ur-Shulgi's pogrom and Sabbat attacks on the holdings of both Independent Clans throughout the world. This has not yet broken The Promise, though may do so in the future.</li> </ul>From an out of game perspective, we plan to offer:<ul><li>Lots of character options for vampires and ghouls, including allowances for rare character types such as Lasombra Antitribu, as well as Camarilla, Anarch and Independent/Autarkis options. For those interested, unfortunately, the Sabbat will be limited to NPCs only.</li> <li>A driven, plot-focused game that will allow PCs to fold into the positions of power in the city (such as Prince, Seneschal and Primogen) as the game ramps up.</li> <li>A tiered play system that allows for three levels of play: heavy socio-political play with more coooperative non-consent focus, less intense political play so those who aren't super-comfortable with the deep politics can dip their toes into it, and a less intensive option for those who wish to eschew political plots and have a little bit more control of what happens to their character.</li> <li>Utilization of events from the greater Masquerade timeline and allowing our players to interact with those events and potentially alter the outcomes.</li> </ul>Right now, the game is nearing completion; it's been a long time coming. The grid is complete, the code is nearly done barring a few outliers, and the NPC starting court is mostly written up. I am looking for people who are interested in getting involved in the game from the ground-up in a number of ways, especially people who are familiar with Masquerade and interested in an immersive environment. In particular, I am looking for people who are familiar with Masquerade and have an interest in helping to approve character concepts for the game, as well as those interested in being an idea bouncing board as we get closer to the opening poing.<br /> <br /> Feel free to post your questions here or you can PM me or email me directly at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3d4955585c494f5850484e557d5a505c5451135e5250\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"14607c71756066717961677c547379757d783a777b79\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. We are looking at, barring something unforseen happening, having an opening in late October. I look forward to hearing from anyone who has questions about, or might be interested in assisting with, the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:18:40-07:00","id":853485,"title":"","content":"Is this still a thing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:29:18-07:00","id":855485,"title":"","content":"I would be very interested in this, if it becomes a reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:43:01-07:00","id":856541,"title":"","content":"If you look at the recent changes tab, you can see that the project is still steadily being worked on. I've slowly watched the development as he's worked on it, and even tried to get a hold of him on the site before, but he's never gotten back to me. If this project ever goes live, I'll be there. My own real concern looking through the page is that the rules have been written out verbatim for just about everything in the book. I'm assuming that will be helpful for people, but also BNS might not be too happy with him for it. He should have put the setting up and worried about the players knowing the rules.<br /> <br /> Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}